# Feature 13 — Request Creation & Dashboard Enhancements

## Goal
Improve the request creation flow and dashboard with better 
usability for designers and copy team.

## 1. Drag and Drop Image Upload on Request Creation
- Add drag and drop zone to the screenshot upload area on the 
  new request page
- When user drags images over the upload area, show a visual 
  highlight with "Drop images here" text
- When dropped, add images to the existing upload queue
- Support multiple images dropped at once
- Keep existing click-to-upload button working
- Only accept image files (PNG, JPG, WEBP)
- Show error if non-image file is dropped: 
  "Only image files are supported"
- Also support paste from clipboard (Cmd+V) to attach images

## 2. Copy Suggestions with One Click
- Add a copy icon button next to each generated copy suggestion
- Clicking it copies the text to clipboard
- Show a brief confirmation: "Copied!" that disappears after 
  2 seconds
- Apply to both English and Arabic suggestions
- This lets designers paste directly into Figma without 
  manually selecting text

## 3. Keep Initial Copy Option
- When a designer regenerates a copy suggestion, keep the 
  previous suggestion visible as an option
- Show it as a "Previous suggestion" card below the new one
- Designer can select either the new or previous suggestion
- This way if none of the AI suggestions are good, the designer 
  can type their own copy in a text input and submit that instead
- Add a "Write my own" option per annotation that reveals a 
  text input for custom copy
- Custom copy should be submitted as-is for review

## 4. Multiple String Selection for Review
- Allow designers to select multiple copy strings at once
- Add a checkbox to each copy string row
- Add a "Select all" option at the top
- When strings are selected, show a bulk action bar:
  "X strings selected — Submit selected for review"
- This lets designers submit only the strings they are 
  happy with, not the entire request at once

## 5. Request Dashboard — Requester and Assignee Info
- On each request card in the dashboard show:
  - "Raised by: [displayName or email]" 
  - For Copy Team view: show who submitted it
  - For Designer view: show which Copy Team member last 
    reviewed it (if any)
- On the request detail page, show the same info in the header
- Pull displayName from the users Firestore collection using 
  the uid stored on the request

## After Changes
- Run npm run build to verify no errors
- Update CLAUDE.md
- Commit and push